regions.text:
city place among the books;
age in your unsurrendering looks;

dom thro' a stuttering line;
while I celebrate your worth in rhyme.

enging high your vibrant song of war,
are your grim embattled miners are;

and maimed and ill and poor,
and thro' the Jailbirds' door;

or broken, home or far away;
born and all who die to-day;

who leave the cradle for the mill;
take a million swords to still;

grandest music singer ever sung;
where the bells of death have rung;

heal the heart of man,
heard on earth since song began;

freedom for a coward's pay;
that hears your song and turns away.

FREEDOM
WILKINSON
